# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Secrets belong to the BACKEND container only and never reach the browser.
# Never prefix one with VITE_ — anything with that prefix is inlined into the
# client bundle and is fully public.

# debug | info | warning | error
LOG_LEVEL=info

# console (human-readable, for local dev) | json (for anywhere else)
LOG_FORMAT=console

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- auth
#
# Leave OIDC_ISSUER empty and auth is OFF: every request is "dev-user" and the
# app runs with no accounts anywhere. Set it and the same endpoints start
# requiring a bearer token.
#
# Any OIDC provider works — the backend verifies the token against the issuer's
# JWKS and never learns which vendor it was. WorkOS AuthKit is free to 1M users;
# Clerk has the best drop-in React components; Logto self-hosts.
#
# OIDC_ISSUER=https://your-tenant.example.com
# OIDC_AUDIENCE=your-api-identifier
